{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `raw_proportions`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added top-level data `raw_proportions`, deterministically computed as `to_vector(y) ./ to_vector(n)`, because the original likelihood scored a transformed-data variable and SafeStan requires protected observations to be top-level data identifiers. The original transformed-data computation of `raw_proportions` was removed. The original `y` input is retained but is not scored or used by the safe model. The three sigma priors were split into separate built-in sampling statements and moved before any parameter-dependent computations; this preserves the same prior density as the original vectorized normal statement.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int J;
  array[J] int n;
  vector[J] x;
  array[J] int y;
  real r;
  real R;
  real overshot;
  real distance_tolerance;
  vector[J] raw_proportions;
}
transformed data {
  vector[J] threshold_angle = asin((R - r) ./ x);
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_angle;
  real<lower=0> sigma_distance;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[J] p_angle;
  vector[J] p_distance;
  vector[J] p;

  sigma_angle ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_distance ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);

  p_angle = 2 * Phi(threshold_angle / sigma_angle) - 1;
  p_distance = Phi((distance_tolerance - overshot)
                   ./ ((x + overshot) * sigma_distance))
               - Phi((-overshot)
                     ./ ((x + overshot) * sigma_distance));
  p = p_angle .* p_distance;
  raw_proportions ~ normal(p,
                           sqrt(p .* (1 - p) ./ to_vector(n) + sigma_y ^ 2));
}
generated quantities {
  real sigma_degrees = sigma_angle * 180 / pi();
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":2,"R":3.9574690601146836,"distance_tolerance":6.353929214354509,"n":[4,6],"overshot":4.17523645179571,"r":3.3773637160365495,"x":[6.209842904592216,6.817873800875649],"y":[2,5],"raw_proportions":[0.5,0.8333333333333334]}","protected_variables":["raw_proportions"]}
